<title>GERMANY: German Jan import prices rise 1.0 pct from Dec.</title>
<headline>German Jan import prices rise 1.0 pct from Dec.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> GERMAN TRADE PRICES    Jan 97	Dec 96	Jan 96</p>
<p>IMPORT prices:</p>
<p>    Monthly figure	  +1.0	  +0.8	 +0.4</p>
<p>    Year-on-year	    +2.6	  +2.0	 -1.0</p>
<p>    Index(base 100 1991)  100.0	 99.0	 97.5</p>
<p>EXPORT prices:</p>
<p>    Monthly figure	  +0.4	  +0.1	 +0.2</p>
<p>    Year-on-year	    +0.5	  +0.3	 +0.5</p>
<p>    Index(base 100 1991)  103.9	103.5	103.4</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150  </p>
<p>NOTE - The statistics office cited the strong increase in the dollar against the mark as a reason for the sharp increase in import prices in January.</p>
<p>&quot;In this context it should be noted that the exchange rate of the dollar against the mark was 9.8 percent than a year ago,&quot; the statistics office said in a statement.</p>
</text>
